@startuml mf-02b-commit-dropoff-retreat
' SRS Section II.1.2.2 — Main Workflow: Delivery, part B (Commit, Swap, Drop-off & Retreat)
' Continues from mf-02a-reserve-aim.puml
' Supersedes mf-02b-dropoff-retreat.puml: the slot is now committed at the zone
' gate by a periodic watch, and a late arrival may swap a slot away from a
' reservation that has not been committed yet.
' Business-level vocabulary only; implementation detail belongs in the SDS.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng mf-02b-commit-dropoff-retreat.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam swimlaneWidth 260
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999

title Delivery - Part B: Commit, Swap, Drop-off & Retreat

|#F2F2F2|FMS (openTCS)|
|#FFFFFF|WES|
|#F2F2F2|AGV|

|WES|
start
:Drop-off Commit Watch: every 0.2 s,\ntake every delivering task that has\nno committed slot yet;
note right: Continued from Part A (Reserve & Aim)
repeat
  :Read where the assigned\nvehicle stands;
  backward:Not yet -\nre-check on the next tick;
repeat while (Has it reached the\ndestination zone?) is (Not yet) not (Yes)
:Take exclusive access to\nthe zone's slot map;
if (Where is the vehicle standing?) then (On an entry point\nof the zone - the gate)
  :Re-run the fill rule (BR-11)\nover the slots nobody has\nCOMMITTED, and offer the best;
  note right
    It can still turn into another
    column, so it is re-offered the
    best slot the rule allows - this
    is what makes a **swap** possible
  end note
else (Already inside\nthe zone)
  :Keep its own\nRESERVATION - no swap;
  note right
    It has passed the last point
    from which another column
    was still reachable
  end note
endif
if (Does the fill rule\noffer a slot?) then (No)
  :Release the zone and log a warning;\nthe next tick tries again;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
#B5E6B5:**COMMIT** the slot on the cargo\nand drop its reservation;
note right
  A committed slot is final - it can
  never be taken away again. Missing
  the tick at the gate is not an error:
  the commit simply happens later and
  loses the right to swap.
end note
:Release the zone;
if (Was that slot another\ncargo's RESERVATION?) then (Yes)
  #FFE699:**SWAP** - re-reserve the displaced cargo\nonto the next slot the fill rule offers;
  #FFE699:Withdraw and re-issue that cargo's drop-off\norder at its new slot, and count the swap;
  note right
    Only an uncommitted reservation can be
    swapped away. The zone was capacity-checked
    when the request was created, so a replacement
    is normally free; where none is, the loss is
    logged and the cargo waits for a later tick.
  end note
else (No)
endif
if (Is the committed slot the\none this vehicle was aimed at?) then (No)
  :Withdraw and re-issue this vehicle's\ndrop-off order at the committed slot;
else (Yes)
endif

|FMS (openTCS)|
:Route the vehicle\nto the committed slot;

|AGV|
:Unload the cargo\nat the slot;

|FMS (openTCS)|
:Notify WES that the cargo\nhas been unloaded;

|WES|
:Record that the cargo\nhas been unloaded;
note right
  The task is STILL DELIVERING -
  the retreat steps are running
end note

|AGV|
:Retreat 2 cells\nclear of the slot;
note right
  So it does not block the
  vehicles queued behind it
end note

|FMS (openTCS)|
:The drop-off transport order\nreaches FINISHED;

|WES|
:Task -> DELIVERY_COMPLETED;\nCargo -> DELIVERED;
stop

legend bottom
|<#B5E6B5>    | **COMMIT** - binding: the slot can never be taken away from this cargo again |
|<#FFE699>    | **SWAP** - the slot is taken from another cargo's uncommitted reservation, which is re-aimed |
endlegend

@enduml
